{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact Question summary head 7ff8d4cb60adba4febf763d3df7361da3b43f888 on builder/question-summary-budget-20261104, tree 3dd4044d, for request 18d6dc0f under promise 24b0c627 and review request 6808b2dc. This approval covers apps/views/src/decision.ts, its owner apps/views/test/s4.test.mjs, the note and the three manifests. It claims no deployment, no host acceptance and no Goose size limit.\n\nScope. Main d372812e is an ancestor, and the worktree is clean. The commit-message check passes for all 3 commits. The head touches apps/views/src/**, a card path. Card run 41799181039 passes at the source commit 2bd1ab4b, and the two later commits add only the note and the three manifests.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- The fix measures the page that Open returns. The adapter now builds the detail card with the item reasons, which is exactly the card the item page returns, and refuses only when that card exceeds 60 KiB. Before, it measured a card that held the full body together with the longer summary reasons. A detail that fitted could therefore read as incomplete on the summary page, which then offered no Open.\n- The summary carries no hidden text. For page summary with text over the first-card bounds, the adapter drops the body and the actions. It keeps the identity, at, actor, actorLabel and projection. ViewSessions already removed actions from a summary without wholeText (session.ts:153), so the empty action list changes no offered act. Short text and every other page keep the earlier card. The item page's reasons and actions don't change.\n- The summary check after the detail check is defensive. A summary without a body of 601 or more characters can't exceed a detail that fits.\n- The owner reaches the boundary through the real adapter and ViewSessions, with ASCII and with multibyte text and JSON escapes. It checks a detail of exactly 61,440 canonical bytes, a ready summary with Open, no body, no actions and no wholeText, and the retained identity fields. Open must return the exact body with approve and request-changes. One more byte refuses both pages, and the session's summary then offers no Open.\n- The control is real. On unchanged source the new case fails at \"A detail that fits remains reachable\" with actual incomplete, expected ready. The repaired owner passes 26 of 26 cases, and its compiler exits 0. The pinned hashes of decision.ts and s4.test.mjs equal the head's files.\n\nValidation history. The stopped launcher and the preliminary runs stay retained, and the record labels them as superseded. Only the owned runs support the claims.\n\nThe gate passed. At 2bd1ab4b, gate.exit reads exit 0. All five stages pass: kernel, 135 Node, 56 Counting, 3,614 plain with one skip, and 1,070 Native with two skips. before.json and after.json match, with a clean status and lockfile 5a717d43…, which equals the committed lockfile. The receipt lists no owned process still present.\n\nEvidence. All 45 public files match their sizes and digests and are read-only. All four SHA256SUMS files match, no unit holds an unlisted file, and the credential scan finds no match. All three manifests name checkpoint 2bd1ab4b. The 39 selected gate originals and the 2,276-file private inventory match, all at mode 0400.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The budget belongs to the page that shows the text, and the session's guard on acts stays the single place that gates them.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The summary now sends less to the host: no body and no acts.\n\nSimplification: no required change.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:95355e684ad94776eb427d23a9b13e1b194eb671","binding":"assigned","head":"7ff8d4cb60adba4febf763d3df7361da3b43f888","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bed6698ea09c83b77016cc7b1485b2697869019d\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:24b0c6278602cfb8c8f1533b8c82238b61a492e2\"]","r